# Integration wave 2 verification (2026-09-17, integrator)

Re-run, unmodified, in the isolated copy (engine `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`):

    $ "$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/input_a11y_audit.gd
    PASS 117/117
    exit=0                                    SCRIPT ERROR lines: 0

One downstream consumer now exercises this contract for real: `screen_menu_audit.gd`
attaches `UiFocusBridge` to the mounted `MenuScreen` and asserts that the screen's nine
`focus_controls()` reach the bridge, that `set_focus("menu/PlayButton")` lands, and that a
confirm `InputEventKey` dispatch routes to `modes`. That is a smoke use, not new audit
coverage of UIR-05; the API itself is unchanged.
